# Sentry + Jira workflow (agent-side)

We do **not** use the paid Sentry↔Jira integration. The agent keeps both systems in sync via MCP.

**Sentry org:** `glowout` (region `https://de.sentry.io`)  
**Jira:** `glowout.atlassian.net` · project **KAN** (GlowOut) · prefer issue type **Bug** for errors

## Before bug / error / “something’s broken” work

1. Search **Sentry** (`search_issues`) for matching unresolved issues — prefer `environment:production`, sort by freq when relevant.
2. Search **Jira** for related open tickets (summary/error text, Sentry short IDs like `GLOWOUT-CLIENT-3Q`).
3. Tell the user what you found before coding.
4. **Reuse** existing tickets. Only create a new Jira Bug when none fits.
5. When creating or linking:
   - Put the Sentry URL in the Jira description.
   - Remote-link Jira → Sentry (`jira-work-item-links-jira-work-item-remote-link`).
   - Add a Sentry issue note with the Jira browse URL.

Skip this search only for pure features/refactors with no error or regression signal.

## When shipping a fix

1. Include both IDs in the commit/PR body, e.g. `Fixes GLOWOUT-CLIENT-3Q` and `KAN-6`.
2. Resolve the Sentry issue (`update_issue`) and note the PR/commit.
3. Transition the Jira ticket toward Done; comment with what changed + PR/commit link.
4. Do **not** resolve either side until the fix is committed (or the user explicitly asks to close without shipping).

## Side work / drive-by fixes

If work might touch an area that already errors in prod, run the Sentry/Jira search first and link the fix to those tickets instead of leaving orphan commits.
